  "quote": "I believe that growth should move all asset production to Content Engine. I see no point in having a separate repository produce specific assets.",
  "note": "Every asset kind to its producer under Krish's 26 Nov 2026 ruling (CHANGES.md): content-engine makes every asset, captions and titles included, from its v5 Library (covers and thumbnails: python scripts/covers/make_covers.py <piece> --out <folder>; carousels: python scripts/library/make_piece.py <piece> --set <set>), and hands Growth finished, approved assets with their captions in the piece manifest. Growth makes nothing: it posts, schedules, places the weekly edition in Substack, distributes, runs the subscribe route, measures, learns, keeps mix.json and the experiments, and reports performance back. It supersedes the 27 Oct Canva lane (growth-canva) and the growth-copy captions of 19 Nov. engine/run/invariants.py:check_production_boundary refuses anything below that comes back; docs/plans and docs/history are dated records and exempt.",
